.TH mouser-engine-bundle 1  "mouser-engine-bundle 1.5.0" 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH NAME
mouser\-engine\-bundle \- Engines: copy Mouser\*(Aqs engine libraries from a build folder into `OUT/<name>/` with their engine.toml (what packages ship); see docs/release.md
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmouser engine bundle\fR [\fB\-\-from\fR] [\fB\-\-yes\fR] <\fB\-\-out\fR> [\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fB\-\-wait\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH DESCRIPTION
Engines: copy Mouser\*(Aqs engine libraries from a build folder into `OUT/<name>/` with their engine.toml (what packages ship); see docs/release.md
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-from\fR \fI<FROM>\fR
Folder with the built libraries (default: beside this mouser)
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Install or update without asking (the card\*(Aqs answer is yes)
.TP
\fB\-\-out\fR \fI<OUT>\fR
Where to put `<name>/` (e.g. `engines` beside the packaged mouser)
.TP
\fB\-\-version\fR \fI<VERSION>\fR
The version to install (a GitHub tag or what the lock pins)
.TP
\fB\-\-wait\fR
Wait for the download to finish (the CLI always does; for scripts)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBmouser\fR(1)
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH VERSION
v1.5.0
